    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 29th with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who occupies the top spot against Pallante. His elite sprint speed, combined with a favorable platoon advantage (+14%) and the opposing pitcher's slow delivery, makes him the premier catalyst for our stolen base production. Joining him in the top tier are **Yordan Alvarez** (73.90) and **Junior Caminero** (73.43). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our most reliable anchor against Crow, while **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from Ure\u00f1a\u2019s 4.58 xERA and a potent +14% boost from his SP skill matchup. We are also capitalizing on **Kazuma Okamoto** (67.98), who draws a favorable park shift (+16%) against Rogers, and **Christian Yelich** (65.69), whose dynamic platoon edge provides a stable floor in the leadoff spot.\n\nOur tactical deployment of **Trea Turner** (62.08) and **Kyle Schwarber** (60.36) against Wrobleski is predicated on the combination of a wind-aided environment and the lefty-lefty matchup, which the model projects will yield high-leverage scoring opportunities. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) rounds out the strong starts, buoyed by a substantial 14% park factor boost. The most difficult decision at the margins involved **Carson Benge** (50.59), who was the first cut from the active lineup. While **Carson Benge** possesses an attractive leadoff spot and favorable wind conditions, the optimizer favored the higher efficiency scores of **Dillon Dingler** (56.77) and **Chase Meidroth** (56.92) due to their superior platoon matchups. We remain cautious of **Luke Raley** (53.16) and **Caleb Durbin** (52.44); while they provide value, their scoring is tempered by tough opposing pitchers and, in the case of **Caleb Durbin**, a significant penalty for the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time. We continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and **Colt Keith**, who is not in the confirmed lineup.",
